# DateTime Boundaries — What Does NOT Create a Date

These expressions should NOT parse as dates. They demonstrate
the boundaries of CalcMark's date type system.

## Bare numbers are never dates

year = 2019
not_a_date = 2025
also_not = 1990

## Date+time in a single literal is not supported

meeting = Apr 1 2019 12:30PM
event = January 15 2026 3:00 PM

## CY/FY/Q notation not yet implemented

cy_test = CY2019
fy_test = FY26
q_test = Q1

## Fiscal without frontmatter produces error

fq_test = FQ1
fiscal_test = this fiscal quarter
